><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250702083057+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250702083108+10'00'" name="2550c039-c158-46a5-a1ed-92eb1d1c2754" page="13" coords="233.670135,93.110672,559.270752,93.110672,233.670135,80.896698,559.270752,80.896698,166.394012,80.557678,559.272034,80.557678,166.394012,68.343704,559.272034,68.343704" rect="166.012329,67.962021,559.653687,93.492355" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14b: yes there were practical reflections on the outcomes of the study</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="13" rect="595.276001,1.110672,779.276001,93.110672"
/></highlight
><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20250702083153+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="2550c039-c158-46a5-a1ed-92eb1d1c2754" date="D:20250702083153+10'00'" name="397c0f78-8923-4fc4-a0f8-7927e91e6284" icon="Comment" page="13" rect="166.012329,69.492355,190.012329,93.492355" subject="Sticky Note" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>To advance the field of medical supplement use by athletes, focus should&#xD;be directed towards improving the quality of the literature specific to high-performance</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>female athletes and with better methodologies to characterise menstrual cycle phase/status.&#xD;Indeed, poor quality was exemplified by a universal lack of consideration for participant&#xD;menstrual status combined with few studies evaluating sexual dimorphisms. While female&#xD;athletes were well-represented in the evidence underpinning iron and vitamin D&#xD;supplementation, there remain some unexplored nuances among athletic populations.&#xD;Investigation of calcium supplementation among female athletes, however, is particularly&#xD;lacking. We note that our findings do not suggest that women should not follow current&#xD;sports nutrition supplementation guidelines to prevent or treat diagnosed clinical&#xD;issues.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="13" rect="595.276001,1.492355,779.276001,93.492355"
/></text
></annots
